      <marc:subfield code="a">‘Eṉṉai Maṉṉippāyā Cātaṉā?’ by Anuradha Chandrasekhar explores the intricacies of marriage and its impact on life through 34 compelling chapters. The novel examines the experiences of intercaste couples and the legal processes surrounding marriage annulments. It emphasizes the importance of addressing ego early on to prevent it from growing into a larger issue. Through engaging dialogues and insightful observations, the book illustrates how acceptance and simplicity can help navigate life&apos;s challenges.</marc:subfield>
